%% One job: the job item's status. Writers: C = baas run, H = its shutdown hook (disarmed once a
%% --detach launch is confirmed, ADR 0007), T = baas jobs terminate (any operator), I = the instance's user-data, W = the instance's watchdog.
%% Every write after the reservation is a conditional UpdateItem that never replaces a terminal status.
%% completed and failed:<n> are written only by I, and a timed-out the CLI did not write only by W: after
%% any of them no CLI path terminates the instance, which ships its log and ends itself (ADR 0003, amended).
%% Only cancelled makes a CLI terminate a live instance it did not stop itself.
%% Never stored, computed by readers: vanished (non-terminal, no live tagged instance, created at least
%% 5 min ago — jobs list and the poll), status-lost (as vanished but measurements exist — the poll only). baas run --format json
%% reports the status it ended with as jobStatus -- or, under --detach, launched (launching if that
%% write was lost), since a detached job has not ended when the CLI exits.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    state "launching" as Launching
    state "launched" as Launched
    state "running" as Running
    state "completed" as Completed
    state "failed:#lt;n#gt;" as Failed
    state "timed-out" as TimedOut
    state "cancelled" as Cancelled
    state "launch-failed" as LaunchFailed

    [*] --> Preflight
    Preflight --> Refused: format, type, managed arguments, JAR not a file,<br/>unreleased build without --runner-jar, no prefix, project, tags,<br/>timeout under 1 s, margin under 60 s, no image, stack outputs missing,<br/>pinned runner release unverifiable · or a --dry-run, which launches nothing
    Refused: Refused — nothing uploaded, no item
    Preflight --> Launching: C reserves the item, before any upload (N3)<br/>— a failed reservation uploads nothing
    Launching --> Launched: C, after the upload and RunInstances (only while still launching)
    Launching --> LaunchFailed: C, upload or RunInstances error (+ launch-error.txt)
    Launching --> Running: I, when C's launched write was lost or late
    Launching --> Cancelled: H Ctrl+C during the upload or mid-launch · T
    Launched --> Running: I, after the watchdog starts
    Launched --> Cancelled: H · T
    Launched --> TimedOut: C poll cap · W
    Running --> Completed: I, exit 0
    Running --> Failed: I, exit n (124 = process timeout)
    Running --> TimedOut: C poll cap · W
    Running --> Cancelled: H · T
    Cancelled --> [*]: a late I running write is refused →<br/>instance ships its log, terminates, never benchmarks
    Completed --> [*]: a late C launched write is refused → confirmed, not cancelled
    Failed --> [*]
    TimedOut --> [*]
    LaunchFailed --> [*]
